# instance/config/channels.yml — org-domain classification for channel
# adapters (AX-5, axes spec docs/plans/cabinet-axes-spec-2026-07-05.md §4).
#
# Every framework/channels adapter resolves classify(recipient) ->
# internal|external from THIS file: a recipient whose email domain equals
# (or is a subdomain of) an entry below classifies `internal`; EVERYTHING
# else — unknown domains, opaque chat/channel ids, malformed handles —
# classifies `external`, the most restrictive class (external recipients
# stay per-item Captain-approved in every posture).
#
# FAIL-CLOSED: an absent file, a symlinked/traversal path, an unknown key,
# a wrong version, or ANY malformed entry loads as the EMPTY domain list —
# every recipient then classifies external until the file is repaired.
# Never best-effort-parsed.
#
# SECURITY: adding a domain WIDENS classification (external -> internal
# action_types), so treat this file like the posture ruling — live
# deployments should add instance/config/channels.yml to the germline lock
# set (cabinet/scripts/germline-lock.sh) so growing it takes the Captain's
# unlock ritual.
#
# Copy to instance/config/channels.yml and replace with your org's domains.
version: 1
org_domains:
  - example.com        # subdomains (mail.example.com) match implicitly
  - example.org
